{
  "requirement": "Usage MUST record each provider request's outcome and available input/output\ntoken counts, including retries, with cached or reasoning-token counts when\nprovided. Missing measurements MUST be recorded as unavailable, not zero.\nRun totals MUST include request and tool-call counts by tool, elapsed time, and\navailable token usage, identifying incomplete totals without double counting\nprovider counters that overlap.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: the requirement is met.** I could not inspect the Rig crate source, so one point rests on an assumption (see the end).\n\n**Implementation**\n\n- **Per-request records, including retries.**\n  - `assess` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` calls `usage.begin_request()` before every provider attempt. It calls `usage.end_request(...)` after every attempt, including timeouts and errors that are then retried.\n  - Each retry therefore gets its own `RequestUsage` entry with an outcome (`unfinished`, `completed`, `failed`, or `cancelled` via `finish`), elapsed time and `TokenCounts`.\n  - Bedrock SDK retries are disabled in `bedrock_sdk_loader` (`src/authoring/providers.rs`), so no attempt is hidden inside one recorded request. The Ollama comment says Rig's transport has no hidden retry layer.\n- **Token counts and unavailable values.**\n  - `TokenCounts::from_usage` copies Rig's `Option<u64>` fields: input, output, cached input, cache-creation input and reasoning.\n  - A failed or unanswered request records `TokenCounts::default()`, which is all `None` and serializes as null, not zero.\n  - A measured zero stays `Some(0)`, so the two cases are distinguishable.\n- **Run totals.**\n  - `UsageRecord` carries `request_count`, `tool_call_count`, per-tool `tool_calls` (plus `tool_failures` and `tool_skipped`), `elapsed_ms` and aggregate `tokens`.\n  - `UsageLog::tool` and `skipped_tool` count calls by tool name, and `tool_name` buckets unknown names as `unknown`.\n  - `elapsed_ms` is refreshed at begin, end and finish.\n  - `TokenCounts::sum` and `sum_counter` return `None` when a counter has no measurements, keep measured subtotals when only some requests report, and set `complete = false` when any request lacks input or output, or when an optional counter is reported by only some requests.\n  - The comment in `sum` says cache and reasoning counters are subsets and are never added into the input or output totals, so overlapping counters are not double counted.\n- **Marking.** All the relevant code carries `{impl}` for this requirement. Extra fields such as tool failures and skips and the content-free `unknown` bucket belong to `usage_storage` and `usage_inputs`, which the same code also implements.\n\n**Tests**\n\n- `src/authoring/usage.rs`\n  - `token_totals_keep_subsets_separate_and_missing_counters_unknown` checks summing, in-flight incomplete totals and a failed request with null tokens.\n  - `partial_failure_retains_available_totals_and_optional_measurements` checks partial totals, a null optional counter, a measured zero, and mixed reporting giving `complete == false`.\n  - `cancelled_request_persists_elapsed_time_and_incomplete_totals` covers the cancelled outcome.\n  - `completed_requests_and_the_run_record_elapsed_time` covers request and run elapsed time.\n  - `tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text` covers per-tool counts.\n  - `failed_submission_can_be_confirmed_on_a_later_attempt` covers a failed then a completed attempt.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs`\n  - `throttled_requests_retry_unchanged_and_record_every_attempt` checks that 9 attempts are recorded (8 failed with `tokens.complete == false`, then 1 completed).\n  - `unanswered_requests_are_abandoned_and_retried` and `success_resets_backoff_and_retries_keep_history_without_repeating_tools` cover timeout retries and a retry after a tool turn.\n- `src/authoring/providers.rs`: `bedrock_sdk_retries_are_disabled` checks `max_attempts == 1`.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs` and `tests/authoring_batch.rs` check end-to-end Ollama and Bedrock runs.\n  - Totals come out as input 22, output 14 and 2 requests for Ollama, and 38, 10 and 2 for Bedrock.\n  - Per-tool counts and failures, and a denied read that fails the run after 1 request, are also checked.\n\n**Residual risk.** I could not verify that Rig's Ollama and Bedrock adapters report absent counters as `None` and not as zero, or that its input counter already includes cached tokens. The code correctly treats Rig's `Option` fields as authoritative and the tests exercise that handling. I judge this adequate and found no acknowledged FIXME gaps.",
